<!--
  B.3 EID-13 pack: children of stock rule 61615 (Sysmon event 13, a registry
  value set) and of its one level-0 child, hand-ported from the Sigma YAML in
  phase-b-detection/sigma/. Phase B ISA F4. IDs 100400 to 100404 here; the
  other B.3 rules sit in their own pack files.

  How the port reads (each construct is in phase-b-detection/CONSTRUCTS.md):
    - every matcher is pcre2 and case-insensitive, as a Sigma string match is
    - |contains is an unanchored pattern and |endswith ends in $
    - |contains and |endswith on one field (100403) are one ordered pattern.
      Sigma lets the two overlap on the one backslash between them, so the
      pattern takes a separator, then anything or nothing, then the value name
    - "not 1 of filter_*" on TargetObject (100401) is one negated field with
      both filters joined. TargetObject is on every event 13, so a negated
      field is safe there
    - |contains|all is a run of lookaheads, one per needle, so the needles
      match in any order as Sigma has them
    - a filter on Details that Sigma writes as null, '' or '(Empty)' (100402)
      is written the other way round, as a positive test. Wazuh drops an
      EventData value that is empty, "-" or "(NULL)", so an empty Details is
      an absent field, and a negated field on an absent field never matches.
      The rule asks for a Details that is present and is not "(Empty)". That
      is what the three filters leave, with one loss: Wazuh also drops a
      Details of a literal "-" or "(NULL)", so the rule is silent on those
      two where Sigma would alert. Whether Sysmon ever writes either is not
      established. Two cases pin the silence
    - a dollar sign before a closing parenthesis is written \z, so the rule
      loader has nothing to read as a variable
    - the decoder hands a rule each backslash of a path doubled, so a separator
      inside a path is written \\+ (one backslash or more). Sigma wants exactly
      one, so a path with a doubled separator in the live event also matches
    - the group names nothing a stock if_group matches. Stock rules attach to
      group sysmon_event_13 by if_group (92300, 92304, 92307), and a pack rule
      in that group would take them as children and lose the final match to
      them
    - every rule names two parents, 61615 and 92300. Wazuh tries a parent's
      level-0 children first, and stock 92300 is the one level-0 child of
      61615 (any value under a Run, RunOnce or Terminal Server Run key), so an
      event that lands on one of those keys and also matches a pack rule would
      end at 92300 with no alert unless the pack rule hangs from it as well.
      None of the five patterns can match a Run path except a value that is
      named for the pattern (a Run value called UserInitMprLogonScript, in
      100400), so for four of the five the second parent is the idiom only.
      The other stock children of 61615 are not level 0: 92304 (level 6,
      ms-settings or Folder shell open command), 92307 (level 3, a .exe under
      Services) and 92308 (level 3, a CLSID LocalServer). They alert rather
      than swallow, so no pack rule needs them as parents
    - under one parent Wazuh tries the higher level first, and at the same
      level the rule loaded first, and the first match is final. Under 92300,
      stock 92301 (level 12, .lnk, .vbs or .vba in Details under a Run key)
      and 92303 (level 12, VNC or tvnserver.exe in Details under a Run key)
      are final over a pack rule that also matches that event. The event
      still alerts, under the stock rule, and a case pins each. Stock 92302
      (level 6, reg.exe under a Run key) is below every pack rule here

  WARN: what the port drops. 100401 lacks upstream's filter_optional_cutepdf,
  which tests Image, TargetObject, Details and User at once. A Wazuh rule holds
  no OR across fields, so "not (A and B and C and D)" cannot be written, and
  keeping only the TargetObject part would hide any DLL written under that
  key name. The rule therefore alerts when CutePDF Writer registers its
  monitor (spoolsv.exe writing cpwmon64_v40.dll). The case
  phase-b-detection/tests/100401/pos-cutepdf.json keeps the cost visible.

  WARN: blind to a WOW6432Node path in 100402. Upstream matches
  \SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\..., and a 32-bit process writes under
  \SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Microsoft\Windows NT\..., which neither rule matches.
  The port keeps the upstream needle.

  Lint: bun tools/sigma-lint.ts. Tests: bun tools/logtest.ts (ISA ISC-130).
-->
<group name="local,eid13_pack,">

  <!-- SigmaHQ 9ace0707: the UserInitMprLogonScript value runs a script at logon. -->
  <rule id="100400" level="10">
    <if_sid>61615, 92300</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.targetObject" type="pcre2">(?i)UserInitMprLogonScript</field>
    <description>EID 13 pack: the UserInitMprLogonScript registry value was set.</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1037.001</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

  <!--
    SigmaHQ 944e8941: a port monitor DLL under Control\Print\Monitors.
    The two single-field filters are one negated TargetObject: the MONVNC
    driver value, and the VNC printer (three needles, any order). The CutePDF
    filter needs four fields and is not here; see the WARN above.
  -->
  <rule id="100401" level="10">
    <if_sid>61615, 92300</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.targetObject" type="pcre2">(?i)\\+Control\\+Print\\+Monitors\\+</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.targetObject" type="pcre2" negate="yes">(?i)\\+Control\\+Print\\+Monitors\\+MONVNC\\+Driver|^(?=.*Control\\+Print\\+Environments\\+)(?=.*\\+Drivers\\+)(?=.*\\+VNC Printer)</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.details" type="pcre2">(?i)\.dll$</field>
    <description>EID 13 pack: a DLL was set under Control\Print\Monitors.</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1547.010</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

  <!--
    SigmaHQ dfb5b4e8: a value under AppCompatFlags InstalledSDB or Custom.
    Details must be present and must not be "(Empty)"; the lookahead ends at
    \z because Details cannot be tested for absence any other way.
  -->
  <rule id="100402" level="10">
    <if_sid>61615, 92300</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.targetObject" type="pcre2">(?i)\\+SOFTWARE\\+Microsoft\\+Windows NT\\+CurrentVersion\\+AppCompatFlags\\+(?:InstalledSDB|Custom)\\+</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.details" type="pcre2">(?i)^(?!\(Empty\)\z).+</field>
    <description>EID 13 pack: a value was set under AppCompatFlags InstalledSDB or Custom.</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1546.011</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

  <!--
    SigmaHQ c7dcacd0: AutoShareWks or AutoShareServer set to 0 under
    LanmanServer\Parameters. The contains and endswith on TargetObject are one
    pattern.
  -->
  <rule id="100403" level="10">
    <if_sid>61615, 92300</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.targetObject" type="pcre2">(?i)\\+Services\\+LanmanServer\\+Parameters\\+(?:.*\\+)?AutoShare(?:Wks|Server)$</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.details" type="pcre2">(?i)^DWORD \(0x00000000\)$</field>
    <description>EID 13 pack: AutoShareWks or AutoShareServer was set to 0.</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1070.005</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

  <!--
    SigmaHQ 48437c39: EnableLUA set to 0. The needle is a contains, as
    upstream has it, so a value name that only starts with EnableLUA matches.
  -->
  <rule id="100404" level="10">
    <if_sid>61615, 92300</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.targetObject" type="pcre2">(?i)\\+Microsoft\\+Windows\\+CurrentVersion\\+Policies\\+System\\+EnableLUA</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.details" type="pcre2">(?i)^DWORD \(0x00000000\)$</field>
    <description>EID 13 pack: UAC was disabled by setting EnableLUA to 0.</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1548.002</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

</group>
